# Implementation Plan: Sovereign Portable Core Consolidation

This plan outlines the "compilation" and migration of the core Sovereign Intelligence components into the standalone `quantum-portable` project.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This will overwrite any legacy logic in `quantum-portable` with the new high-fidelity Gemini 3 / Oracle 3.0 suite.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component: Intelligence Core Migration]

#### [NEW] [quantum_core.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/quantum-portable/swarm/core/quantum_core.ts)
- Port the latest Oracle 3.0 logic from `appforge-main`.
- Integrate the high-speed quantum simulation engine.

#### [NEW] [gemini_skill_adapter.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/quantum-portable/swarm/core/gemini_skill_adapter.ts)
- Port the Gemini 3 SDK adapter for high-fidelity reasoning.

#### [NEW] [hyper_brain.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/quantum-portable/swarm/core/hyper_brain.ts)
- Port the Hyper Intelligence expert routing middleware.

### [Component: Orchestration]

#### [NEW] [QUANTUM_LAUNCHER.bat](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/quantum-portable/QUANTUM_LAUNCHER.bat)
- Create a standalone batch script to initialize the portable core and a CLI interface.

#### [NEW] [package.json](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/quantum-portable/package.json)
- Define a lightweight dependency list (only `@google/genai`, `socket.io-client`, etc.) for portability.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
- Run a `portable_benchmark.ts` within the `quantum-portable` folder to ensure the core resolves correctly.

### Manual Verification
- Verify that double-clicking `QUANTUM_LAUNCHER.bat` initializes the Oracle without errors.
